From 19b7ab2410117e71ecb040495d556ca059d9b800 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devon Tuma <dtumad@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 18:24:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] try the simp route before rfl in the localLength_eq
 default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rfl default whnf-unfolds the entire bind chain of main: on a
17-operation circuit that is 334k heartbeats (~15s) of silent cost at
instance elaboration, invisible in the source. The circuit_norm simp route
proves the same goal in 2.4k heartbeats and still falls back to rfl for
circuits the simp set cannot flatten. Small circuits close in the simp
branch too (~160 heartbeats), so nothing regresses.

(The channelsLawful default has a related problem — it fails outright on
channel-heavy mains, forcing hand-written full-simp workarounds downstream —
but the right fix there needs the sub-circuit channel lemmas investigated
first; not touched here.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Clean/Circuit/Basic.lean | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Clean/Circuit/Basic.lean b/Clean/Circuit/Basic.lean
index 2ff1e543..04fcbb1b 100644
--- a/Clean/Circuit/Basic.lean
+++ b/Clean/Circuit/Basic.lean
@@ -212,9 +212,16 @@ class ElaboratedCircuit (F : Type) (Input Output : TypeMap) [Field F] [CircuitTy
   /-- how many local witnesses this circuit introduces -/
   localLength : Var Input F → ℕ
 
-  /-- the local length must not depend on the offset. usually automatically proved by `rfl` -/
+  /-- the local length must not depend on the offset. The default tries the `circuit_norm` simp
+  route before `rfl`: on non-trivial `main`s, `rfl` whnf-unfolds the whole bind chain (measured
+  334k heartbeats on a 17-operation circuit vs 2.4k for the simp route). -/
   localLength_eq : ∀ input offset, (main input).localLength offset = localLength input
-    := by intros; rfl
+    := by
+      intros
+      try dsimp only [main]
+      first
+        | (simp +arith only [circuit_norm, seval]; done)
+        | rfl
 
   /-- a direct way of computing the output of this circuit (i.e. without having to unfold `main`) -/
   output : Var Input F → ℕ → Var Output F := fun input offset => (main input).output offset
-- 
